# Production App Reverse-Engineering Playbook

> A repeatable workflow for rebuilding a production-grade application from a real production app as reference.

## Core Principle

**Do not rebuild screens. Rebuild the system that makes those screens possible.**

The overall journey:

```text
REFERENCE APP
     ↓
1. OBSERVE
     ↓
2. MAP
     ↓
3. TRACE USER JOURNEYS
     ↓
4. DISCOVER DOMAIN
     ↓
5. DISCOVER STATE & RULES
     ↓
6. DESIGN SYSTEM
     ↓
7. BUILD FOUNDATION
     ↓
8. BUILD FIRST VERTICAL SLICE
     ↓
9. VALIDATE ARCHITECTURE
     ↓
10. EXPAND
     ↓
11. HARDEN
     ↓
12. FINISH
```

---

# PHASE 0 — DEFINE THE CHALLENGE

Before touching the codebase, define what you're trying to reproduce.

## Reference

```text
App:
Platform:
Purpose:
Why I chose it:
```

## Scope

```text
I WILL reproduce:
-

I WILL NOT reproduce:
-

Target quality:
-

Definition of done:
-
```

## Important

The goal is **not**:

```text
Recreate the original source code.
```

The goal is:

```text
Recreate the important behavior,
architecture properties,
reliability,
state management,
and production qualities.
```

