# ONE SENTENCE TO REMEMBER

> **Observe the behavior → understand the system → design ownership and boundaries → build one complete flow → validate → expand → harden.**

### For your Asuken project specifically

Your **next action is only Phase 1**.

Don't create the architecture yet. Don't create `AuthModule`, `DietModule`, `SocialModule`, etc. yet.

Create these three files first:

```text
asuken/
├── 01-observation.md
├── unknowns.md
└── 02-system-map.md   # leave mostly empty for now
```

Then spend your first pass **only observing Asuken**. Once observation is reasonably complete, you move to the system map. This prevents you from falling back into your old “identify modules → immediately code them” cycle.

